# port-patches.sh: glm/sampling-r7 @ 3c8b05d8bbb7 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 2cb4f1d2ccf8..f4bdb3247840); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
core + server + glm_cuda lanes: a prompt with pictures is kept and resumed under its content key; a pass attaches its pictures once, every mark's segment injects them, a resumed pass runs the tower only for the pictures past its cut (TF_GLM_IMAGE_CACHE, TF_GLM_IMAGE_MARK_SNAP)

A prompt with pictures or clips held the image placeholder (154854) at every
picture row, so its ids alone would let two different pictures share a kept
state, and such a prompt was never kept: the lane host skipped its lookup,
marks, keeps and disk probe. Port of the DeepSeek Zig port's picture work
(its recipe 0006's content keys, which GLM did not have) into GLM's shapes.

- core/prompt_media.zig (new; re-exported by prompt_cache): Media (a span and
  the full SHA-256, the same bytes as core/spill's format.Media), pictureId
  (format.pictureId's scheme 1), itemDigest (SHA-256 of `image[3, H, W]` or
  `video[T, 3, H, W]`, a zero byte, then the canvas bytes: Python's
  FittedPicture head), keyOf (the keyed prompt and one identity an item; none
  for features from another tower, a follower's copy, or an item whose rows
  are not one run), mediaKeys, spansMatch, historyLen, snapMarks, and the two
  switches' readings.
- engine_api.Request: cache_key and cache_media beside media; server
  prompt.zig keyMedia keys the zig vision backend's prompt when the engine has
  a prompt cache and TF_GLM_IMAGE_CACHE is not "0", its history the prompt
  before the template's generation prompt (never inside a picture); the python
  backend (features only) stays unkeyed.
- lane_host: keyOf/cacheable/tierMedia (cache_media counts only when item i's
  rows are exactly media i's span); the admission lookup, the marks' keeps,
  the warm pass, parkOwn's probe and restore and holdPass key by the content
  key; keepInfo carries the pictures and the model ids; a picture request
  joins no other conversation (0111 is text only). TF_GLM_IMAGE_MARK_SNAP=1:
  a mark inside a picture moves back to the grid at its start.
- prompt_cache: Want.images/media, Write.images/media/raw, KeepInfo's,
  Store.probeMedia; Entry.images: such a state is never a conversation's
  continuation and never goes to the v1 disk tier.
- glm_cuda lanes + engine: pass() attaches the stream's media once
  (Engine.attachPass) at its resume point, hands them to every segment
  (marks and the last) with hold_media and detaches them when it ends (also
  on an error); startPass attaches at its own resume point unless a pass
  did, before the MTP head enters; attachMedia runs the tower only on the
  items with a row at or past the cut (Media.neededFrom, Python's rule),
  their features at their own rows' offsets; media_skipped counts the rest.
  Under TF_GLM_FILL=1 a picture prompt still runs pass() whole at its begin,
  so the same holds there. The broadcast to rank 1 and its mirror record are
  unchanged.

Switches: TF_GLM_IMAGE_CACHE (on; only "0" turns it off: picture prompts
keep and resume nothing, as before), TF_GLM_IMAGE_MARK_SNAP (off; "1": no
kept state cuts inside a picture). With the prompt cache off (the engine's
default) nothing changes for any request; with it on, text requests are
unchanged and picture requests are now kept and resumed in memory.

Tests (host): prompt_media (key scheme, Python's digest head, keyOf,
historyLen, snapMarks); prompt_cache_media_test (lookups and keeps carry the
identities and the model ids, a disk hit resumes, two different pictures at
the same rows never share a state, unbound or unkeyed media keep nothing,
0111 skips picture states, the mark snap); Media.neededFrom; a pass over
pictures attaches once, every segment sees them, a resume at 128 runs the
tower from the third picture; a picture prompt refused before its sequence;
the same under TF_GLM_FILL=1 with marks on both ranks.

Measured on the pair: not run yet (a picture conversation resumed in memory
equal to a cold prefill, two same-size pictures at the same rows missing,
the tower's determinism for a straddling cut).

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); the DeepSeek Zig
port's picture work and the Python GLM engine's FittedPicture keys.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0027-zig-glm-pictures.patch

